<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmose I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1550–1525 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmose I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Eighteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a> around 1550 BCE. He completed the expulsion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and reunited the country. His reign marks the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, the period of the Egyptian Empire's greatest expansion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmose-i.jpg" alt="Ahmose I" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_of_Ahmose_I_MET_DP140854.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
